The Basics
One player is chosen to run the game (Host). They will not play and instead run the game. In the game, everyone receives a role card, which they may not show to any other players and must place face-down in front of themself. The game has a cycle of two phases: night and day, starting with night.
At night all players must close their eyes while the Host calls on certain players/roles to perform an action.
During the day all players may open their eyes and discuss. At the end of the day (ends at Host discretion), one player is chosen to be lynched. All players must vote at the same time by pointing at who they wish to lynch. Whoever receives the most votes is eliminated. In case of a tie, nobody dies.